.\" milog(1) — single-host nginx + system + app-error monitor
.\"
.\" This man page is hand-written roff. To preview locally:
.\"   man -l man/milog.1
.\" Or:
.\"   nroff -man man/milog.1 | less
.\"
.\" Every command in src/dispatch.sh needs an entry under COMMANDS;
.\" tests/smoke_docs_drift.sh fails CI when one is missing.
.\"
.TH MILOG 1 "2026-10-03" "milog" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
milog \- single-host nginx + system + app-error monitor with alerts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B milog
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR ...]
.br
.B milog
[\fB-h\fR | \fB--help\fR | \fBhelp\fR]
.br
.B milog
\fICOMMAND\fR
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmilog\fR ships as a single bash bundle plus optional Go binaries
(\fBmilog-web\fR, \fBmilog-tui\fR). It tails nginx access logs, the
systemd journal, docker container logs, and arbitrary text logs from one
host, computes per-app metrics, and fires alerts to Discord, Slack,
Telegram, Matrix, generic webhooks, and user-defined hook scripts.
Bash modes work on any POSIX box with bash 4+; Go binaries unlock the
SSE web dashboard, the bubbletea TUI, and the Prometheus
\fB/metrics\fR endpoint.
.PP
The default invocation
.RB ( "milog" )
tails every configured source with a coloured prefix per source. All
other behaviour is opt-in through a subcommand.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Live views
.TP
.B monitor
Bash dashboard \(em refresh-and-redraw TUI showing CPU / MEM / DISK +
per-app nginx tables. Keys: \fBq\fR quit, \fBp\fR pause, \fBr\fR refresh,
\fB+\fR/\fB-\fR change rate.
.TP
.B tui
Richer Charm Bubble Tea TUI in Go, with contextual key help, focused
views for alerts / paths / errors / trends, and predictable navigation
for longer lists. Same data as
.BR monitor .
Requires the
.B milog-tui
companion binary on
.BR PATH .
Keys include \fBq\fR quit, \fBp\fR pause, \fBr\fR refresh,
\fB?\fR help, arrows/\fBk\fR/\fBj\fR select, enter/\fBl\fR drill in,
arrows/\fBk\fR/\fBj\fR scroll focused views, \fBf\fR/page-down and
\fBb\fR/page-up page, and esc/\fBh\fR/backspace return.
.TP
.B rate
Nginx-only req/min dashboard.
.TP
.B web
Read-only local HTTP dashboard. Subcommands: \fBstart\fR, \fBstop\fR,
\fBstatus\fR, \fBinstall-service\fR, \fBuninstall-service\fR,
\fBrotate-token\fR. Prefers the
.B milog-web
Go binary (SSE + Prometheus
.BR /metrics )
when present, falls back to a bash
.BR socat (1)
poller otherwise.
.TP
.B daemon
Headless rule evaluator + alerter. No TUI. Refuses to start when
.B milog config validate
reports errors; warnings are allowed.
.SS Per-app inspection
.TP
.B health
Per-app totals \(em 2xx / 3xx / 4xx / 5xx counts, plus the share of
requests from AI crawler user-agents (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, …).
.TP
.BR top " [\fIN\fR]"
Top \fIN\fR source IPs across all apps (default 10). Ends with the
AI-crawler share of all requests. Adds a country
column when
.B GEOIP_ENABLED=1
and
.BR mmdblookup (1)
is on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BR top-ip-by-app " [\fIN\fR]"
Top \fIN\fR source IPs per app (default 5). Alias:
.BR top-by-app .
.TP
.BR top-paths " [\fIN\fR]"
Top \fIN\fR URLs by req / 4xx / 5xx / p95. Excludes
.B SLOW_EXCLUDE_PATHS
(WebSocket paths by default).
.TP
.B attacker " \fIIP\fR"
Forensic view of one IP across apps \(em per-app requests, top paths,
top user-agents, classification, sample lines. Adds a CrowdSec reputation
line when
.B CROWDSEC_CTI_KEY
is set.
.TP
.BR slow " [\fIN\fR]"
Top \fIN\fR slow endpoints by p95. Requires
.B $request_time
in nginx
.BR log_format ;
excludes WebSocket paths.
.TP
.BR ws " [\fIN\fR]"
WebSocket session metrics \(em duration distribution, longest, long-session
flag, top paths per app.
.TP
.B stats " \fIAPP\fR"
Hourly request histogram for one app.
.TP
.BR trend " [\fIAPP\fR] [\fIHOURS\fR]"
Sparkline from history (requires
.BR HISTORY_ENABLED=1 ).
.TP
.B diff
Per-app: now vs 1d ago vs 7d ago.
.TP
.BR auto-tune " [\fIDAYS\fR]"
Suggest threshold values from history data, plus a threshold raise or a
silence for each rule averaging more than 10 fires a day in alerts.log.
Prints commands; applies nothing.
.TP
.B replay " \fIFILE\fR"
Postmortem for one archived log file.
.SS Search and filter
.TP
.B logs
Tail every configured source with a coloured prefix per source. Same as
running
.B milog
with no command.
.TP
.B search " \fIPATTERN\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR]"
Grep across current + archived log files.
Flags:
.BR --since ,
.BR --app ,
.BR --path ,
.BR --regex ,
.BR --archives ,
.BR --limit .
.TP
.BR errors " [\fIFLAGS\fR]"
Live tail (default) or summary report (\fB--since\fR /\fB--source\fR
/\fB--pattern\fR). Live mode: nginx sources show 4xx/5xx, others show
app-pattern matches. Summary mode: scans
.B alerts.log
for
.B app:<src>:<pat>
fires within the window.
.TP
.B exploits
Live tail of LFI / RCE / SQLi / XSS / infra-probe payload hits.
.TP
.B probes
Live tail of scanner / bot user-agent traffic.
.TP
.BR patterns " [\fBlist\fR]"
App-error pattern detector across all sources. Built-ins: Go panic,
Python traceback, Java stacktrace, Node UPR, OOM, segfault,
ERROR/FATAL/CRITICAL.
.B milog patterns list
shows the merged catalog (built-ins + overrides + custom).
.TP
.B grep " \fIAPP\fR \fIPATTERN\fR"
Filter-tail one app.
.TP
.BR suspects " [\fIN\fR] [\fIWINDOW\fR]"
Heuristic bot ranking. IPs with a cached CrowdSec reputation get a
.BI CS: reputation
flag.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config
Show resolved config + destinations + apps (no args).
.br
Subs: \fBshow\fR, \fBpath\fR, \fBinit\fR, \fBedit\fR, \fBadd\fR \fINAME\fR,
\fBrm\fR \fINAME\fR, \fBdir\fR \fIPATH\fR, \fBset\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR,
\fBvalidate\fR.
.TP
.B alert " \fISUB\fR"
Toggle alerting + systemd service. Subs: \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR, \fBstatus\fR,
\fBtest\fR, \fBstats\fR [\fIWINDOW\fR] (fires per rule from alerts.log,
default \fB7d\fR).
.TP
.BR alerts " [\fIWINDOW\fR]"
Fire history reader. Window grammar: \fBtoday\fR, \fByesterday\fR,
\fBall\fR, \fIN\fBm\fR, \fIN\fBh\fR, \fIN\fBd\fR, \fIN\fBw\fR (default
\fBtoday\fR).
.TP
.B silence " \fIRULE\fR \fIDURATION\fR [\fIMESSAGE\fR]"
Mute a rule. Also: \fBsilence list\fR, \fBsilence clear\fR \fIRULE\fR.
.TP
.BR digest " [\fIWINDOW\fR]"
Exec-summary for the period.
.TP
.BR report " [\fIWINDOW\fR] [\fB\-\-html\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]"
Static report for the window (default \fB7d\fR; same grammar as
\fBdigest\fR): requests, 4xx and 5xx per app, the top 10 IPs by 4xx
responses, alert fires per rule, and anomaly alerts. Markdown by default;
\fB\-\-html\fR prints one self-contained HTML page with no scripts. Writes to stdout, or
to \fIFILE\fR with \fB\-o\fR.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnostic checklist \(em flags every degraded optional capability with a
one-line fix.
.SS Host audit
.B audit
runs point-in-time integrity scans. It reads no log files. Baselines and
scan state live under
.IR ~/.cache/milog/audit/
(\fBALERT_STATE_DIR\fR/audit). With no subcommand, prints help. Each
scanner defaults to \fBstatus\fR when its subcommand is omitted.
\fBcheck\fR and \fBscan\fR exit 1 when they find drift or new matches,
and when they cannot run (no baseline yet, \fByara\fR missing).
.TP
.B audit fim " \fBbaseline\fR | \fBcheck\fR | \fBstatus\fR"
SHA256, mtime, and size of each path in
.BR AUDIT_FIM_PATHS .
.B check
reports paths that were modified, removed, appeared, or became unreadable
since the baseline.
.TP
.B audit persistence " \fBbaseline\fR | \fBcheck\fR | \fBstatus\fR"
New files under
.B AUDIT_PERSISTENCE_PATHS
(default: cron directories and spools, systemd units and timers,
.IR /etc/rc.local ,
.IR /etc/ld.so.preload ).
.B check
lists removed files too but exits 1 only for new ones.
.TP
.B audit ports " \fBbaseline\fR | \fBcheck\fR | \fBstatus\fR"
TCP and UDP listeners read from
.BR ss (8),
or
.BR netstat (8)
when
.B ss
is missing.
.B check
exits 1 only for new listeners.
.TP
.B audit yara " \fBinit\fR | \fBscan\fR | \fBstatus\fR"
.B init
writes default rules to
.B milog-default.yar
in
.B AUDIT_YARA_RULES_DIR
(default
.IR ~/.config/milog/yara ).
.B scan
runs
.BR yara (1)
over
.B AUDIT_YARA_PATHS
and prints matches not reported before. Needs the
.B yara
binary and a non-empty
.BR AUDIT_YARA_PATHS .
.TP
.B audit accounts " \fBbaseline\fR | \fBcheck\fR | \fBstatus\fR"
Line-level diff of the files in
.B AUDIT_ACCOUNTS_PATHS
(default:
.IR /etc/passwd ,
sudoers, and root and
.I /home/*
authorized_keys files).
.B check
exits 1 only for added lines.
.TP
.B audit rootkit " \fBcheck\fR | \fBstatus\fR"
Heuristics: more PIDs in
.I /proc
than
.BR ps (1)
lists (by more than 5), an
.I /etc/ld.so.preload
file, processes running from
.IR /tmp ,
.IR /var/tmp ,
or
.IR /dev/shm ,
and processes whose executable was deleted. Linux only;
.B check
exits 1 on other systems.
.TP
.B audit history " [\fIdays\fR]"
Drift that
.B milog daemon
stored in the history database over the last
.I days
(default 7), newest first. Needs
.B HISTORY_ENABLED=1
and
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.PP
When
.B AUDIT_ENABLED=1
and
.B milog daemon
is running, each scanner runs on its
.B AUDIT_*_INTERVAL
timer and fires an
.B audit:<scanner>:...
alert on drift. The fim, persistence, ports, and accounts scanners
record a baseline on their first run instead of alerting. With
.B HISTORY_ENABLED=1
each finding is also stored in the history database (a finding that
persists across checks is stored once), for
.B audit history
and the TUI integrity view.
.SS Kernel observability
.TP
.B probe " \fBstatus\fR | \fBinstall-service\fR | \fBuninstall-service\fR"
Manages the
.B milog-probe
eBPF sidecar (Linux only) as the systemd unit
.IR /etc/systemd/system/milog-probe.service .
.B status
shows whether the unit is active.
.B install-service
needs root: it writes the unit, sets
.B HOME
and
.B MILOG_CONFIG
to the invoking user's so alerts use that user's config, and runs
.BR "systemctl enable --now" .
.B MILOG_PROBE_FILE_ALLOWLIST
overrides the default file-event allowlist written into the unit.
.B MILOG_PROBE_BIN
overrides the binary path.
.B uninstall-service
needs root and stops, disables, and removes the unit.
With no subcommand, prints help.
.SS Distribution
.TP
.B install " \fIFEATURE\fR"
On-demand feature installer. Features:
.BR geoip ,
.BR web ,
.BR history .
.B install list
shows installed state.
.TP
.B update-rules
Download
.B milog-rules.tsv
from the latest release of
.B MILOG_RELEASE_REPO
(default chud-lori/milog), check its SHA-256 against that release's
.BR checksums.txt ,
check that every regex compiles, and write it to
.B RULES_FILE
atomically. Refuses a version lower than the active rules. The checksum
file comes from the same release, so this detects corruption, not a
compromised release; it is not a signature.
.TP
.B completions " <\fBinstall\fR | \fBbash\fR | \fBzsh\fR | \fBfish\fR>"
Install / print shell completion script.
.TP
.BR bench " [\fB--full\fR] [\fB--baseline\fR \fIFILE\fR]"
Synthetic-fixture timing harness for CI baseline comparison.
.SH GLOBAL HELP
.TP
.BR "milog help" ", " "milog --help"
List all commands (slim main help).
.TP
.B milog \fICOMMAND\fR --help
Detailed per-command help block (usage / args / 1\(en2 examples).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/milog/config.sh
User config file (sourced as bash). Override path with
.BR MILOG_CONFIG .
Template via
.BR "milog config init" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/milog/rules.tsv
Default
.BR RULES_FILE :
exploit and probe detection regexes written by
.BR "milog update-rules" .
When absent or invalid, the rules built into milog apply.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/milog/
Default
.B ALERT_STATE_DIR
\(em holds
.BR alerts.log ,
.BR alerts.state
(cooldown timestamps),
.B alerts.fingerprints
(cross-rule dedup),
.BR alerts.silences ,
and the CrowdSec CTI cache
.I cti/
with its last failure in
.BR cti.err .
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/milog-web.service
Web dashboard user unit (written by
.BR "milog web install-service" ).
.TP
.I /var/log/nginx/<app>.access.log
Default per-app log location. Override
.B LOG_DIR
to change.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every config variable has a matching
.BR MILOG_ *
override. Common ones:
.TP
.B MILOG_CONFIG
Alternate config file path (default
.IR ~/.config/milog/config.sh ).
.TP
.B MILOG_LOG_DIR
Override
.BR LOG_DIR .
.TP
.B MILOG_APPS
Space-separated list, overrides
.BR LOGS .
.TP
.B MILOG_ALERTS_ENABLED
Master alert switch. Set to
.B 1
to fire alerts.
.TP
.B MILOG_PATTERNS_ENABLED
App-error pattern detector switch (default
.BR 1 ).
.TP
.B MILOG_DISCORD_WEBHOOK ", " MILOG_SLACK_WEBHOOK ", " MILOG_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
Per-destination credentials.
.TP
.B MILOG_CROWDSEC_CTI_KEY
CrowdSec CTI API key, overrides
.BR CROWDSEC_CTI_KEY .
When set,
.BR attacker ,
.BR suspects ,
and exploit and probe alerts show the IP's CrowdSec reputation; lookups
are cached for 24 hours. Empty means no requests to CrowdSec.
.TP
.B MILOG_DOCKER_ROOT
Docker state dir for
.B docker:
sources when
.BR docker (1)
inspect is unavailable (default
.IR /var/lib/docker ).
.PP
See
.B milog config
for the complete env-var table.
.SH LOG SOURCES
The
.B LOGS
array names log sources. Four prefixes are recognised; bare names default
to nginx.
.TP
.BR api ", " nginx:api
Nginx app at
.IR $LOG_DIR/api.access.log .
.TP
.B text:\fINAME\fR:\fIPATH\fR
Arbitrary text log at the absolute
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B journal:\fIUNIT\fR
Systemd journal for
.IR UNIT
\(em streamed via
.BR journalctl (1)
.BR -f .
.TP
.B docker:\fICONTAINER\fR
Docker container's JSON log file, unwrapped on read via
.BR jq (1)
or
.BR sed (1).
.PP
Streaming, filtering (\fBlogs\fR, \fBgrep\fR, \fBsearch\fR, raw
\fBmilog \fIname\fR tail) work uniformly across all four source types.
Parsing modes (\fBmonitor\fR, \fBtop\fR, \fBslow\fR, \fBtop-paths\fR,
alerts, web dashboard) require nginx combined-log format.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error \(em invalid arguments, unknown command, broken config, missing
required tool. Diagnostic on stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Bash dashboard with default refresh:
.B milog monitor
.TP
Live tail of all sources, coloured per source:
.B milog
.TP
Top 20 source IPs in the last hour:
.B "milog top 20"
.TP
Filter-tail one app for a pattern:
.B "milog grep api timeout"
.TP
Recent app-pattern fires across every source:
.B "milog errors --since 1d"
.TP
Mute a noisy rule for 1 hour:
.B "milog silence app:api:panic_go 1h \(dqdeploying fix\(dq"
.TP
Web dashboard as a systemd user service:
.B "milog web install-service && systemctl --user start milog-web"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR jq (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR nginx (8).
.PP
